WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.010
For reasons best known to herself...

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:58.620
Marilla did not tell Anne that she was to stay
at Green Gables, until the next afternoon.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:08.170
During the forenoon she kept Anne
busy with various tasks,

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:13.520
and watched over her with a
keen eye while she did them.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.470
By noon...

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:23.150
She had concluded that Anne was smart and
obedient, willing to work and quick to learn.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:27.490
Her most serious shortcoming seemed
to be a tendency to fall into daydreams

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.480
in the middle of a task and forget all about it,

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:35.150
until such time as she was sharply recalled
to earth by a reprimand or a catastrophe.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.100
Oh, please, Miss Cuthbert,

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.400
won't you tell me if you are going
to send me away or not?

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.470
I've tried to be patient all the morning,

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.670
but I really cannot bear
not knowing any longer.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.370
You haven't scalded the dishcloth in
clean hot water as I told you to do.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.460
Just go and do it before you
ask any more questions.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.920
Well, I suppose I
might as well tell you.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.250
We have decided to keep you.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.900
That is, if you will try to be a good
little girl and show yourself grateful.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.820
Why, whatever is the matter?

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.310
I'm crying.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.020
I can't think why.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.900
I'm glad as glad can be.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.820
Oh, glad doesn't seem the right word at all.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.530
I was glad about the White
Way and the cherry blossoms...

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.680
But this!

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.390
Oh, it's something more than glad.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.370
I'm so happy.

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:11.740
I'll try to be so good.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.400
It will be uphill work.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.750
However, I'll do my very best.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.490
But can you tell me why I'm crying?

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:26.230
I suppose it's because you're
all excited and worked up.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.440
Sit down on that chair and try to calm yourself.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.790
I'm afraid you both cry and laugh far too easily.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.870
Yes, you can stay here,

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:40.110
and we will try to do right by you.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:40.980
Welcome!

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:41.410
You must go to school,

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.320
Anne! Come out and play!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.360
but it's only a fortnight till
vacation so it isn't worth while

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.220
Come out and play!

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:46.330
but it's only a fortnight till
vacation so it isn't worth while

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:46.670
for you to go before
it opens again in September.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:50.990
welcome! Anne, come out!

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.240
Anne! come out and play! Welcome!

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.230
Where are you going?

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:59.770
I'm going to say hello to Snow Queen,
and tell it I'm staying here.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:00.500
Wait!

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:01.930
I'll be back soon!

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.670
Good afternoon, Snow Queen!

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.660
Good afternoon, all trees
and friends of the forest!

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.200
Good afternoon!

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.060
Everyone, I'm very pleased to meet all of you!

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.520
Anne!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:36.560
Mr. Cuthbert! Mr. Cuthbert!

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:42.610
Mr. Cuthbert, I can stay in Green Gables now!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:50.740
Miss Cuthbert...

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.850
Miss Cuthbert decided to let me stay.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:01.820
Well now, well now.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:09.420
Mr. Chuthbert, all the words you
told me on the carriage came true.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.530
Mr. Cuthbert, I feel like I'm dreaming.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.860
Well now!

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:22.030
It's not a dream!
It's not a dream!

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:29.220
You're right Anne. This isn't a dream.
You're Anne of Green gables now.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.460
Mr. Cuthbert!

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.360
Thank you, Mr. Cuthbert.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:45.020
Anne!

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.030
Where did she go?

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.220
She said she would be back soon.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:59.670
We have to be stricter on her.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:04.710
Well, I can't blame her. She had
hoped to live a life like this.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.320
Can I pluck it?

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.130
Of course.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.560
I'll put it in a vase as a decoration.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.080
Where have you been until just now?

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.090
Didn't you hear me calling you?

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.790
I'm sorry Miss Cuthbert!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:43.740
Because I was too happy, I went
to greet the woods and the brook.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.670
Everyone welcomed me so much...

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.310
and I forgot the time.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:54.340
I understand how you feel,

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:58.010
but I have a lot to tell you.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:01.080
You said you would be back soon.

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:05.440
If you can't be responsible for
your words, you can't stay here.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.890
Are your feet clean?

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:10.880
Yes!

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:14.170
Then help me set the tea
after washing your hands.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.170
Yes!

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:14.750
Miss Cuthbert. How should I
address Mr. Cuthbert and you?

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.050
Shall I always say Miss. and Mr. Cuthbert?

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:21.680
Can I call you Aunt Marilla?

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.700
No, you'll call me just plain Marilla.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:27.690
I'm not used to being called Miss. Cuthbert
and it would make me nervous.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.170
But It sounds awfully
disrespectful to just say Marilla.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:38.510
I guess there'll be nothing disrespectful
in it if you're careful to speak respectfully.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:43.870
I'd love to call you Aunt Marilla.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:48.930
I've never had an aunt or any relation at all,
not even a grandmother.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.800
If I call you Aunt Marilla,

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:54.150
it would make me feel as if
I really belonged to you.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.630
Can't I call you Aunt Marilla?

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:01.210
No. I'm not your aunt and
I don't believe in calling

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.070
people names that don't belong to them.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:09.000
But we could imagine you were my aunt.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.590
I couldn't.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.030
Do you never imagine things different
from what they really are?

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:16.780
No.

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:20.020
Oh, how much you miss!

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:24.930
I don't believe in imagining things
different from what they really are.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:31.340
Mr. Cuthbert, could I call you uncle Matthew?

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:33.160
Well now.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:38.310
I guess you'd better call me Matthew.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.080
Really?

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:51.000
Anne, after the tea, follow me
to where our animals are.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.820
There are cats there.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.190
Oh! Cats? I want to see them!

00:14:55.440 --> 00:15:01.820
No. After the tea you have to
memorize your prayers.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:05.210
There's to be no more of such
praying as I heard last night.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:07.850
I understand.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:11.830
Since I'm staying here,
I can see the cats anytime.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.190
Well now, you're right.

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:42.050
Do you think that I shall ever have
a bosom friend in Avonlea?

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.460
A... a what kind of friend?

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.140
A bosom friend... An intimate friend, you know...

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:52.360
A really kindred spirit to whom
I can confide my inmost soul.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:58.770
I've dreamed of meeting her all my life.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.080
So many of my loveliest dreams have come
true all at once that perhaps

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.290
this one will, too.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:06.970
Do you think it's possible?

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:13.340
Diana Barry lives over at Orchard Slope
and she's about your age.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:15.890
She's a very nice little girl

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:18.160
and perhaps she will be a playmate
for you when she comes home.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:21.540
She's visiting her aunt over
at Carmody just now.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.140
You'll have to be careful how
you behave yourself, though.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.020
Mrs. Barry is a very particular woman.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:31.770
She won't let Diana play with any
little girl who isn't nice and good.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.400
What is Diana like?

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.660
Her hair isn't red, is it?

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:40.840
Oh, I hope not. It's bad
enough to have red hair myself,

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:44.540
but I positively couldn't endure it
in a bosom friend.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.430
Diana is a very pretty little girl.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:53.800
She has black eyes and hair,
and rosy cheeks.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:58.050
And she is good and smart,
which is better than being pretty.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.290
Oh, I'm so glad she's pretty.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:09.580
Next to being beautiful oneself...
and that's impossible in my case.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.050
It would be best to have a
beautiful bosom friend.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:21.460
When I lived with Mrs. Thomas she
had a bookcase  with glass doors.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:24.020
But there weren't any books in it.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:30.440
One of the doors was broken by Mr.
Thomas one night when he was intoxicated.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.600
But the other was whole,

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:36.660
and I used to pretend
that my reflection in it...

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:40.460
was another little girl who lived in it.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:47.950
I called her Katie Maurice,

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.470
and we were very intimate.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:55.910
I used to talk to her by the hour,
especially on Sunday,

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:58.690
and tell her everything.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.730
Katie was the comfort and
consolation of my life.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:06.070
We used to pretend
that the bookcase was enchanted.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.160
And that if I only knew the spell,

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:14.890
I could open the door and step right into
the room where Katie Maurice lived.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:19.110
And then Katie Maurice would
have taken me by the hand,

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:24.530
and led me out into a wonderful place,
all flowers and sunshine and fairies

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:28.800
and we would have lived there
happy for ever after.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:02.970
When I went to live with Mrs. Hammond,

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:06.660
it just broke my heart
to leave Katie Maurice.

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:15.890
She felt it dreadfully, too.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.640
I know she did,

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:24.820
for she was crying when she kissed me
goodbye through the bookcase door.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:30.810
Stop imagining those things.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.120
I don't approve of such goings-on.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:37.730
You seem to half believe
your own imaginations.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:40.480
It will be well for you to have

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.500
a real live friend to put such
nonsense out of your head.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.550
Now, go into the sitting room

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:49.810
and bring me out the illustrated
card that's on the mantelpiece.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:51.730
You must memorize your prayers well.

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.650
I suppose my prayer last night
was very awkward

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.570
but, it was my first time.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.940
You couldn't expect me to pray
very well, could you?

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:04.190
I thought out a splendid prayer after I went
to bed, just as I promised you I would.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:06.180
It was very poetical.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:10.580
But I couldn't remember one word
when I woke up this morning.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:15.260
And I'm afraid I'll never be able to
think out another one as good.

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:16.690
listen to me, Anne.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:20.750
When I tell you to do a thing I
want you to obey me at once,

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:23.160
and not stand stock-still and
discourse about it.

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.430
Now, go.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:56.180
Our Father who art in heaven
hallowed be Thy name.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:01.450
May Thy kingdom come, Thy will
be done in earth, as it is in heaven.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:05.280
I like this, It's beautiful.

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:10.350
Our Father who art in heaven
hallowed be Thy name.

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.240
That is just like a line of music.

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.800
It looks like as long as you have
someone to talk to, you won't stop.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.990
Take the ilustrated card
to your room to learn.

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:24.100
Oh, I know it pretty nearly all now...
all but just the last line.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.020
Just do as I tell you.

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:30.420
Remember to memorize it well.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:37.600
Can I take the apple blossoms
with me for company?

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.920
No. I dont want your room
cluttered up with flowers.

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:44.670
You should have left them
on the tree in the first place.

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:48.280
I did feel a little that way, too.

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:53.140
I kind of felt I shouldn't shorten their
lovely lives by picking them.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:57.550
I wouldn't want to be picked
if I were an apple blossom.

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:02.300
But the temptation was irresistible.

00:22:02.770 --> 00:22:06.180
What do you do when you meet
with an irresistible temptation?

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:09.100
Anne. Did you hear me tell
you to go to your room?

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:28.200
Forgive our sins, just as we
have forgiven others...

00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:43.680
My name is Cordelia.

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:46.180
Lady Cordelia Fitzgerald.

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:50.530
I am tall and regal, clad in a
gown of trailing white lace

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:54.930
with a pearl cross on my breast
and pearls in my hair.

00:22:56.250 --> 00:23:02.500
My hair is of midnight darkness and
my skin is a clear ivory pallor.

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:07.820
No, I can't make that seem real.

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:18.760
You're only Anne of Green Gables,

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:22.340
and I see you, just as you are looking now

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.730
whenever I try to imagine
I'm the Lady Cordelia.

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:28.980
But it's a million times nicer to be

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:32.190
Anne of Green Gables than
Anne of nowhere in particular, isn't it?

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:36.270
I am Anne of Green Gables!

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:38.400
Anne of Green Gables!

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:42.430
Diana, I hope we can become bosom friends.

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:22.180
Anne was reprimanded by
Mrs. Rachel Lynde, about her red hair.

00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:25.690
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:29.250
Mrs. Rachel Lynde Is Properly Horrified.
Please watch.
